      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T00:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You could think that doing so would make the measurements more accurate.\n\nThinking about it, as long as there is a consistent delay between the actual edge, and the invocation of get_time(), then the measured time elapsed between any to events will still be equally accurate, (and I think that relative time of events is all that we can hope for having precise, as the clock of HyperDebug is not synchronized to anything.)\n\nI have a followup CL in the works, with many optimizations, among those relying only on 32-bit time values in this interrupt handler, as that will work provided that there is never an hour or more between adjacent events.  I would like to decide on the data format and agree that we have handled corner cases for correctness in this review.  Then we can debate optimization tradeoffs in the next one.",
