      "writtenOn": "2023-02-02T00:55:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I will add some explanation of the data format.  Conceptually, it is storing a queue of pairs (diff, signal_no), each pair being encoded as a u64 by shifting the diff left by just enough to allow storing the highest signal_no (usually zero, one or two bits), and putting the signal_no as the least significant bits.  Finally, the sequence of integers are encoded as bytes by putting seven data bits into each byte, with the MSB indicating whether more are to come.\n\nSo in this case, I want to store a diff of zero, which I am doing by not or-ing anything into the higher bits, leaving just signal_no on the lowest bits (I know for sure that this will never exceed 7 bits, so no need to do a while loop to encode as bytes.)",
      "parentUuid": "e36b5126_65640997",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 156,
        "startChar": 2,
        "endLine": 160,
        "endChar": 25
